## Report
Attempted to build/run a workspace PoC with cargo, but offline dependency resolution failed: `cargo run -p auth --bin poc` errored with `failed to get tiny_http as a dependency of package server` due to crates.io access being blocked. Code path shows untrusted policy expiration parsing: `validate_post_policy` calls `check_expiration` (crates/auth/src/post.rs:108-114), which calls `parse_iso8601` and then `date_to_epoch` (post.rs:235-271). `parse_iso8601` parses year/month/day without range checks, and `date_to_epoch` indexes `month_days[m as usize]` for `m in 1..month` (post.rs:263-266), so month > 13 panics; the year loop `for y in 1970..year` (post.rs:260-261) can also be extremely large. To demonstrate the crash despite build constraints, I compiled a standalone PoC (poc_iso.rs) containing the same parsing code and executed it with an invalid month `2025-14-01T00:00:00Z`. This produced a panic: `index out of bounds: the len is 13 but the index is 13` in `date_to_epoch`, confirming the DoS vector via crafted expiration.

